# Smart-X gateway - ready-made requests for testing Part 2.
# Open this file in Visual Studio 2022+ (or VS Code with the REST Client extension) while the API is
# running and click "Send request" above any block. Every request below is also described in the README.

@gateway = http://localhost:5224

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. QUEUES - Queue<T> routine lane vs PriorityQueue alert lane
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### A normal reading: lands in the FIFO routine queue (receipt says "lane": "Routine")
POST {{gateway}}/api/sensors/ESP32-PWR-02/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dataType": "Int", "intValue": 152, "unit": "W" }

### SIMULATE A HIGH-PRIORITY ALERT: a severe power spike (>= 400 W) is routed to the priority lane
### and bypasses everything waiting in the routine queue ("lane": "Alert", "severity": "Critical")
POST {{gateway}}/api/sensors/ESP32-PWR-02/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dataType": "Int", "intValue": 870, "unit": "W" }

### A critical moisture drop (< 20%) on a hydroponics soil probe - also takes the priority lane
POST {{gateway}}/api/sensors/ESP32-SOIL-01/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dataType": "Float", "floatValue": 12.5, "unit": "%" }

### Build a backlog first: the simulated fleet floods 1,200 buffered readings at once,
### with one severe spike hidden halfway through. Then watch the pipeline below.
POST {{gateway}}/api/simulator/storm?packets=1200

### Queue depths, average waits per lane, and how many packets the last alert jumped
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/pipeline

### The event history - look for "viaPriorityLane": true and "bypassed": <n>
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/history?take=20


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. STACK - manual override commands with Undo
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### "Shut down all valves" - one command, every valve recorded on the undo stack
POST {{gateway}}/api/stream/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "TurnOff", "scope": "AllValves" }

### Trigger a water pump
POST {{gateway}}/api/stream/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "TurnOn", "scope": "Device", "deviceId": "ESP32-PMP-01" }

### Undo (pops the stack; LIFO)
POST {{gateway}}/api/stream/commands/undo

### The device shadow the simulated actuators poll for their desired state
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/shadow


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. DICTIONARY / SORTED DICTIONARY - O(1) device lookup and time-ordered timelines
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Register a device by MAC address in any spelling - it is normalised to one dictionary key
POST {{gateway}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "24-6f-28-aa-bb-cc", "location": "Facility A / Grow Room / NFT Channel 3", "category": "Valve", "displayName": "Valve 3" }

### The same device, a different spelling - 409 Conflict, because it is the same key
POST {{gateway}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "24:6F:28:AA:BB:CC", "location": "Facility A / Grow Room / NFT Channel 3", "category": "Valve" }

### A reading stamped 40 seconds in the past arrives late - the SortedDictionary files it in order
POST {{gateway}}/api/sensors/ESP32-ENV-01/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dataType": "Float", "floatValue": 61.5, "unit": "%", "timestampUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 -40 s}}" }

### A device's timeline over the last 5 minutes, already sorted by timestamp ("selectedTimeline" in the snapshot)
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/snapshot?selected=ESP32-SOIL-02&minutes=5


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. SEARCH / FILTER - category and alert-state index sets
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Pumps and valves that are currently Critical or Offline (union within a group, intersection across)
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/devices?category=WaterPump&category=Valve&alert=Critical&alert=Offline

### Free-text search (the text, in any case, anywhere in the name, ID, location or category)
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/devices?q=bay%202

### Log a search for the suggestion engine to learn from
POST {{gateway}}/api/stream/searches
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "Moisture Sensor B" }


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. HASHSET - unique active faults and disconnected nodes
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Cut power to one node for 30 seconds. Expect ONE "went offline" event, then
### "duplicatesSuppressed" climbing on every health sweep until it reconnects.
POST {{gateway}}/api/simulator/outage/ESP32-ENV-03?seconds=30

### Active faults, disconnected nodes, and the running count of suppressed duplicates
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/alerts


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. PREDICTIVE ACTION ENGINE
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Everything the dashboard draws, in one response - "insights" holds the ranked suggestions
### and "patterns" the strongest learned condition -> operator response patterns
GET {{gateway}}/api/stream/snapshot?selected=ESP32-SOIL-02&minutes=5

